    "description": "866-868 33rd Avenue is a VACANT move-in ready Edwardian duplex located in the desirable Central Richmond neighborhood of San Francisco with a great curb appeal. The property comprises two nearly identical units with 2BD/1BA in each unit, beautiful hardwood floors, with both bedrooms overlooking the large backyard, formal living room with a fireplace, formal dining room, eat-in kitchen, a pantry room, and internal access to garage and backyard. Additionally, there is a large garage for a 2-car tandem parking and another parking spot in front of the house, lots of storage, washer/dryer, and a lovely landscaped backyard. This home offers the potential for lower-level expansion and a quick condo conversion. 866-868 33rd Avenue is only half a block away from public transportation, the Golden Gate Park, a short walking distance to Ocean Beach, Lands End, Sutro Baths, Lincoln Park Golf Course, Legion of Honor. Residents can also enjoy the shops, restaurants, and bars just blocks away. Popular neighborhood spots include Cassava, Simple Pleasures, Fiorella, Devil's Teeth Baking, Hook Fish, Pearl 6101, Pizzetta 211, El Mansour, and Hard Knox Cafe. *Some photos have virtual staging."
  },
